{
  "title": "What a Friend We Have in Jesus",
  "author": "Joseph M. Scriven (1819-1886)",
  "key": "F",
  "public_domain": true,
  "arrangement": [
    "Verse 1",
    "Verse 2",
    "Verse 3"
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "label": "Verse 1",
      "kind": "verse",
      "color_hex": "#2378C3",
      "hotkey": "1",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "What a friend we have in Jesus, all our sins and griefs to bear!",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 32,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 59,
              "text": "F"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "What a privilege to carry everything to God in prayer!",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 20,
              "text": "Dm"
            },
            {
              "position": 26,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 47,
              "text": "F"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "O what peace we often forfeit, O what needless pain we bear,",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 22,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 31,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 55,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "All because we do not carry everything to God in prayer.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 22,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 28,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 49,
              "text": "F"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Verse 2",
      "kind": "verse",
      "color_hex": "#2378C3",
      "hotkey": "2",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Have we trials and temptations? Is there trouble anywhere?",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 23,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 52,
              "text": "F"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "We should never be discouraged; take it to the Lord in prayer.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 22,
              "text": "Dm"
            },
            {
              "position": 32,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 55,
              "text": "F"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Can we find a friend so faithful who will all our sorrows share?",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 24,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 33,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 58,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jesus knows our every weakness; take it to the Lord in prayer.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 22,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 32,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 55,
              "text": "F"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Verse 3",
      "kind": "verse",
      "color_hex": "#2378C3",
      "hotkey": "3",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Are we weak and heavy laden, cumbered with a load of care?",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 22,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 53,
              "text": "F"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Precious Savior, still our refuge— take it to the Lord in prayer.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 27,
              "text": "Dm"
            },
            {
              "position": 35,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 58,
              "text": "F"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Do thy friends despise, forsake thee? Take it to the Lord in prayer;",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 27,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 38,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 61,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In His arms He’ll take and shield thee; thou wilt find a solace there.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 27,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 40,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 64,
              "text": "F"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
